hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16536","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was at al-Abwa or Waddan, so I gifted him of the meat of a wild donkey while he was in ihram, so he returned it to me, and when he saw displeasure in my face, he said: It is not our rejection of you, but we are in ihram; and I heard him say: There is no sanctuary except for Allah and His Messenger; and he was asked about the people of a house of polytheists who are attacked by night, and their women and offspring are hit, so he said: They are of them; then al-Zuhri says: Then he forbade that afterwards."
"16537","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi, that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at al-Abwa or Waddan, a wild donkey, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned it to him, and when he saw what was in my face, he said: We did not return it to you except that we are in ihram."
"16538","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: If horses raided by night and hit the children of the polytheists, he said: They are of their fathers."
"16539","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no sanctuary except for Allah and His Messenger."
"16540","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Indeed we hit in night attacks of the offspring of the polytheists, he said: They are of them."
"16541","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me while I was at al-Abwa, so I gifted him a wild donkey, so he returned it to me, and when he saw displeasure in my face, he said: It is not our rejection of you, but we are in ihram."
"16542","He said: Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Sab ibn Jaththamah, that he said: He passed by me while I was at al-Abwa or Waddan, so I gifted him a wild donkey, so he returned it to me, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw displeasure in my face, he said: It is not our rejection of you, but we are in ihram; I said to Ibn Shihab: Was the donkey hamstrung, he said: I do not know."
"16543","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a wild donkey while he was in ihram, then he mentioned it."
